      "summary": "Returns – Conditional Display of Returns Link",
      "description": "Sub-Functional Area:\n My Orders - Returns\nDescription:\n The system will only display the returns link if the order is eligible for a return.\nStatus:\n Under Review\nNotes:\nNotes: This is part of the requirement documentation\nAccenture Additional Notes: Please provide the all business logic rules for when the \"Returns\" link should not be displayed (e.g. is it based on a product attribute / OMS status / delivery mode). How do Narvar & Global-E handle this logic? Does Magento currently send the information?\nZimm Response: First check is whether the order contains items that are returnable - then display the link. This data should be available on the product's attribute. Secondly, depending on the delivery completion date - from the delivery completion date, the customer has 15 days to do the return. If no delivery completion date is available, then show returns link for 28 days from order creation date. This second requirement is third party dependent - we need the delivery date passed back via MuleSoft\nAccenture Notes: Like for like if heavy on dev\nSizing:\n 5 days",
