      "id": "17840",
      "key": "SFCC-14",
      "summary": "Returns & Refunds",
      "description": "Epic Name:\n Returns & Refunds\nEpic Summary\nThis epic covers non-returnable product flagging, returns initiation links in My Account, return and cancellation status display, and return history. SFCC's role is primarily surfacing the correct redirect and displaying status received from NewStore via MuleSoft — actual returns processing is owned by Narvar (domestic) and Global-e (international).\nBusiness Value / Objective\nClear returns messaging and accurate status display reduce CS contacts and set correct customer expectations pre- and post-purchase. For a premium brand like Zimmermann, a frictionless returns experience is a core part of the customer relationship.\nScope\nIn Scope:\nNon-returnable flag at SKU and category level; configurable in BM\nNon-returnable / final sale messaging on PDP, cart, mini-cart, and through checkout\nReturns link on order detail page in My Account (Narvar for domestic; Global-e for international)\nReturns history page in My Account (completed returns only, sourced from NewStore via MuleSoft)\nReturn detail page including taxes and duties display per country\nReturn status display as received from NewStore via MuleSoft\nReturns policy link at checkout\nOrder cancellation, partial cancellation, and BOPIS cancellation status display in My Account\nRefund processed messaging (note about bank processing time, content managed in Contentful)\nOut of Scope:\nReturns processing and portal — Narvar scope (domestic) / Global-e scope (international)\nRefund processing — Adyen/NewStore scope; SFCC displays status only\nOOBO (Order on Behalf Of) — out of scope\nDependencies\nMuleSoft/NewStore OMS — return status, cancellation status, and tax/duties values fed to SFCC for display\nNarvar — domestic returns portal redirect\nGlobal-e — international returns portal redirect\nContentful — configurable messaging for non-returnable items and refund status copy\nAssumptions & Constraints\nSFCC displays return and cancellation status exactly as received from NewStore via MuleSoft — no derivation logic in SFCC\nReturns initiation is fully managed by Narvar (domestic) and Global-e (international); SFCC owns the redirect only\nRefund processed status is not displayed directly to the customer; a configurable note about bank processing time is shown instead",
