      "id": "17839",
      "key": "SFCC-13",
      "summary": "Payments",
      "description": "Epic Name:\n Payments\nEpic Summary\nThis epic covers the payment step of checkout for all domestic storefronts, including payment method display, card and digital wallet processing via Adyen, saved card management, split payment support (gift cards, credit notes, Retail Rewards), fraud management, and tax and duties display. For international storefronts, Global-e owns all payment processing.\nBusiness Value / Objective\nPayment is the final conversion point in the customer journey. Supporting a broad range of localised payment methods, a smooth saved card experience, and robust fraud management ensures Zimmermann can convert customers across all domestic markets while protecting revenue integrity.\nScope\nIn Scope:\nPayment method display at checkout, configured per storefront in BM\nCredit/debit card, PayPal, Apple Pay, Google Pay via Adyen (all domestic storefronts)\nApple Pay Express and Google Pay Express in mini-bag\nKlarna BNPL via Adyen (AU and US)\nSaved card display, save on checkout opt-in, CVV re-entry, and removal via My Account\nSplit payment: gift card/credit note/Retail Rewards combined with any external payment method\nRetail Rewards automatic application and display for Gold/Platinum VIP members\nPay by Link via Adyen for manual/CS orders\n3DS authentication inline via Adyen Drop-In\nFraud management data passing to Adyen RevenueProtect; order hold and release flow via MuleSoft/NewStore\nTax and duties display (GST/VAT/Tax labels, DDP/DDU messaging) across PDP, mini-cart, cart and checkout\nAvalara tax calculation for US domestic, NZ, and New Caledonia\nHS code passing to Global-e (international) and Avalara (cross-border domestic)\nOut of Scope:\nGift card and credit note balance check and redemption — covered in SFCC-17 (Credit Notes & Gift Cards)\nGlobal-e payment processing — Global-e scope for EU international, HK, ME, US international\nAdyen fraud rule configuration — Adyen/Zimmermann scope\nAvalara configuration — Zimmermann scope\nDependencies\nAdyen Drop-In cartridge — all domestic payment processing including Klarna, Apple Pay, Google Pay\nAP21 via MuleSoft — Retail Rewards balance retrieval and validation in real-time\nGiveX via NewStore/MuleSoft — gift card and credit note redemption at payment step\nGlobal-e — international payment handoff; no Adyen invoked for Global-e orders\nAvalara cartridge — tax calculation for US domestic, NZ, New Caledonia\nMuleSoft — fraud event routing between Adyen and NewStore OMS\nAssumptions & Constraints\nSaved card tokens are held in Adyen; SFCC stores token references only — no raw card data\nFraud rule configuration, thresholds and risk scoring are owned entirely within Adyen\nRetail Rewards are treated as a voucher payment method, not a discount; applied before tax for US, post-tax for all other domestic storefronts\nGlobal-e customers on HK, ME, EU international and US international cannot use Adyen payment methods; they are directed to contact Client Services to redeem Retail Rewards\nApple Pay and Google Pay targeting August 2026; Klarna targeting August 2026",
