      "id": "17832",
      "key": "SFCC-6",
      "summary": "Product Listing Page (PLP)",
      "description": "Epic Name:\n Product Listing Page (PLP)\nEpic Summary\nThis epic covers the build of the Product Listing Page in the Zimmermann PWA Kit storefront, including the product grid, filtering, sorting, pagination, and product tile components. It connects to the SFCC category catalogue for navigation-driven browsing and depends on the Einstein Search index configuration delivered in SFCC-7 for facet and filter rendering.\nBusiness Value / Objective\nThe PLP is the primary product discovery surface for Zimmermann customers. A well-built PLP with intuitive filtering and sorting enables customers to find relevant products quickly, directly supporting conversion across all 8 storefronts.\nScope\nIn Scope:\nProduct grid layout (tile display with image, name, price, colour swatches, badges)\nEach colour variant of a product is displayed as a separate tile in the product grid — one tile per colour, each with its own image and independent grid position\nFilter/facet panel rendering (UI component consuming Einstein facet config)\nSort options UI (e.g. Featured, Newest, Price low–high, Price high–low)\nInfinite scroll and/or pagination\nOOS product display rules on PLP (greyed out, hidden, or pushed to end — to be confirmed)\nProduct state indicators on tiles (Coming Soon, Back in Soon, Sale, New badges)\nCategory-driven PLP (navigation from megamenu to category page)\nOut of Scope:\nEinstein search index configuration and facet attribute setup in BM — covered in SFCC-7 (Search & Recommendations)\nSorting and ranking rules configuration in Einstein — covered in SFCC-7\nProduct attribute and data model — covered in SFCC-4 (Product Catalogue)\nPricing display logic — covered in SFCC-18 (Pricing)\nMegamenu and navigation build — covered in SFCC-3 (Homepage & Navigation)\nDependencies\nMuleSoft/AP21 product feed — product data must be flowing into SFCC\nContentful integration — for any editorial content or banners rendered within the PLP\nZimmermann to provide Figma designs for PLP\nZimmermann to confirm full list of filter facets and sort options to be exposed\nOOS display behaviour to be confirmed before build\nAssumptions & Constraints\nCategory-driven browsing uses the SFCC catalogue; search-driven results use Einstein (SFCC-7)\nOOS display behaviour on PLP (hidden vs greyed out vs end of list) is to be confirmed by Zimmermann\nColour swatch source (hex, SFCC-hosted image, or Contentful) is an open item — to be confirmed before build\nRegional variations in sort options or available facets across the 8 storefronts to be confirmed",
