    {
      "id": "17831",
      "key": "SFCC-5",
      "summary": "Product Detail Page (PDP)",
      "description": "Epic Name:\n Product Detail Page (PDP)\nEpic Summary\nThis epic covers the build of the Product Detail Page in the Zimmermann PWA Kit storefront. It includes the imagery gallery, size and colour selection, real-time inventory display, add-to-bag and wishlist actions, product content from Contentful/Vimeo, and supporting features such as size guides, Notify Me, and Find in Boutique. It depends on the product data model configured in the Product Catalogue epic (SFCC-4).\nBusiness Value / Objective\nThe PDP is the primary conversion point for Zimmermann's customers. A well-built PDP that accurately surfaces product information, availability, and imagery directly supports purchase confidence and reduces drop-off. It must reflect Zimmermann's premium brand experience across all 8 regional storefronts.\nScope\nIn Scope:\nProduct imagery gallery (multi-image, zoom, colour variant switching)\nSize and colour selection with real-time per-size inventory display\nOut-of-stock size indication and Notify Me (back-in-stock) trigger\nAdd-to-bag and add-to-wishlist actions\nSize guide display logic\nProduct content rendering (description, attributes sourced from SFCC/AP21)\nVimeo video embed support\nFind in Boutique modal (per-boutique availability, Google Maps, geolocation)\nBuffer stock display logic (buffered inventory feed applied on PDP)\nProduct badges display (e.g. New, Sale, Runway)\nOut of Scope:\nProduct attribute and data model configuration — covered in SFCC-4 (Product Catalogue)\nSorting and filtering — covered in PLP / Search epics SFCC-6, SFCC-7\nInventory list setup and reservation logic — covered in SFCC-11 (Cart)\nPricing display logic and pricebook setup — covered in SFCC-18 (Pricing)\nContent authoring in Contentful \nMuleSoft / AP21 feed development \nDependencies\nMuleSoft/AP21 product feed — product data must be flowing into SFCC before PDP can be tested end-to-end\nContentful cartridge integration — for product content and video URL references\nFigma designs from design team\nOpen decision: Vimeo vs Contentful video hosting approach — must be resolved before PDP component build begins\nAssumptions & Constraints\nAP21 is the source of truth for product data; SFCC renders what it receives via MuleSoft\nTwo inventory feeds are in scope: a buffered feed for PDP stock display and a true physical inventory feed for Find in Boutique\nNotify Me subscriptions are stored in SFCC; the notification trigger mechanism (likely Emarsys) is to be confirmed\nRegional content variations are managed via Contentful's locale model",
