      "id": "17830",
      "key": "SFCC-4",
      "summary": "Product Catalogue",
      "description": "Epic Name:\n Product Catalogue\nEpic Summary\nThis epic covers the configuration of the product data model in Salesforce Commerce Cloud Business Manager, including product attributes, catalogue hierarchy, and category taxonomy aligned to AP21 and PLM source data. It ensures the foundational product structure is correctly set up in SFCC to support all downstream storefront epics.\nBusiness Value / Objective\nA correctly configured product catalogue is the foundation for the entire storefront — PDP, PLP, search, and cart all depend on a well-structured product data model. This epic ensures SFCC accurately reflects Zimmermann's product hierarchy and attribute model sourced from AP21/PLM, enabling consistent product representation across all regional storefronts.\nScope\nIn Scope:\nProduct attribute configuration in BM aligned to AP21 / PLM data model\nCatalogue hierarchy and category taxonomy setup\nProduct variation groups (colour/size)\nProduct feed ingestion and mapping from MuleSoft/AP21\nOut of Scope:\nSorting and filtering attribute setup — covered in SFCC-6 (PLP) or SFCC-7 (Search & Recommendations)\nPLP/PDP frontend build — covered in SFCC-5 and SFCC-6\nPricing and pricebook configuration — covered in SFCC-18\nProduct data migration from Magento — covered in SFCC-20\nDependencies\nSFCC-1 (Platform Setup & Environments) — BM must be provisioned\nMuleSoft integration for AP21/PLM product data feed\nZimmermann to confirm and sign off final attribute model and category taxonomy\nAssumptions & Constraints\nAP21 is the source of truth for product data\nCategory taxonomy is signed off by Zimmermann before BM configuration begins\nProduct feed format and frequency to be confirmed with the integration team",
