    {
      "id": "17842",
      "key": "SFCC-16",
      "summary": "Customer Account & CRM",
      "description": "Epic Name:\n Customer Account & CRM\nEpic Summary\nThis epic covers the full My Account experience including registration, login, account dashboard, address book, saved cards, wishlist, loyalty, communication preferences, and marketing opt-in capture. Customer data is stored in SFCC and kept in bidirectional sync with Omneo as the system of record via MuleSoft. A single global customer account is maintained across all 8 storefronts.\nBusiness Value / Objective\nA seamless My Account experience drives repeat purchase, loyalty engagement, and personalisation. Getting the SFCC–Omneo–AP21 sync right at go-live is critical — it underpins loyalty tier display, Retail Rewards, saved addresses, communication preferences, and VIC customer group access across all storefronts.\nScope\nIn Scope:\nAccount registration, login, password reset, and reCAPTCHA\nMy Account dashboard (welcome message, loyalty status, Retail Rewards summary, recent orders, addresses, wishlist teaser, newsletter status)\nAccount details management (name, email, mobile, password) with Omneo sync\nAddress book (add, edit, remove, default management) with Omneo sync\nSaved cards management in My Account (view, remove, set default) via Adyen token references\nWishlist — add/remove from PLP and PDP at size level, My Account wishlist page, share by email, back-in-stock notifications for wishlist items, global wishlist across storefronts\nLoyalty — legacy VIC tier display and Retail Rewards voucher display (sourced from AP21 via Omneo), new loyalty tier page and benefits display, VIC exclusive product access via private URL and customer group\nAppointments section within My Account (Booksy integration — storefront scope and timelines TBC)\nCommunication preferences page (Omneo iFrame embedded in My Account)\nMarketing opt-in capture at registration, newsletter sign-up, and back-in-stock form — all passed to Omneo\nSingle global account with storefront-level bag separation\nOut of Scope:\nGuest account creation in Omneo at checkout — covered in SFCC-12 (Checkout Flow & Delivery)\nOrder history and order detail display — covered in SFCC-15 (Order Management)\nReturns history display — covered in SFCC-14 (Returns & Refunds)\nSaved card display and selection at checkout — covered in SFCC-13 (Payments)\nCommunication preference management within Emarsys — Zimmermann scope\nLoyalty programme rules and tier configuration — Omneo/AP21 scope\nBooksy platform configuration — Zimmermann scope\nDependencies\nOmneo — system of record for customer identity, loyalty, addresses, and communication preferences; bidirectional sync via MuleSoft\nAP21 — source of Retail Rewards balances and voucher data; queried in real-time via Omneo\nAdyen — saved card token storage and management\nEmarsys — marketing communications triggered via Omneo on opt-in\nBooksy — appointment data source for My Account appointments section (scope TBC)\nMuleSoft — bidirectional webhook for all SFCC–Omneo data sync\nAssumptions & Constraints\nOmneo is the master for all customer profile, address, and communication preference data; SFCC stores data locally and syncs bidirectionally\nA single global customer account is maintained across all storefronts; shopping bags are storefront-specific\nSaved cards are stored in Adyen (token references in SFCC) for domestic storefronts only; not available on EU international, HK, ME and US international storefronts\nWishlist data is stored and managed within SFCC (not Omneo) — enhancement to move to Omneo logged for future release\nAppointments section storefront scope and delivery timelines are TBC pending further scoping with Zimmermann",
