    "content": {
      "value": "Requirements extracted from Zimmermann Functional Requirements excel, downloaded July 3rd, 2026 after all requirements were confirmed. Req ID prefix: **OM**.\n\n⚠️ **Rows with strikethrough are out of scope** — struck through in the Excel source file.\n\n| Req ID | Sub-Functional Area | Requirement | Owner | Storefront | Config/Custom | Status | **Comments** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| OM-001 | Order Creation & Processing | The system will create an order record in SFCC upon successful payment authorisation | Dependent SF Functionality | ALL | Config | Confirmed | Should be de-scoped since this is Adyen behavior @Jasmijn Tsang |\n| OM-002 | Order Creation & Processing | The system will send confirmed orders to MuleSoft upon successful order creation in SFCC. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-003 | Order Creation & Processing | The system will support the Pay at Order Creation model for all domestic storefronts; full payment is captured at placement. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed | Should be de-scoped since this is Adyen behavior @Jasmijn Tsang |\n| OM-004 | Order Creation & Processing | The system will pass all required order attributes to MuleSoft at export: line items, quantities, prices, selected delivery method, addresses, gift card redemption (if applicable), promotional codes, customer group, and packaging preference. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-005 | Order Creation & Processing | The system will display an order confirmation page: order number, item summary, delivery address, selected delivery method, and estimated delivery timeframe. | Dependent SF Functionality | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-006 | Order Creation & Processing | For international orders, the system will receive the confirmed order payload from Global-e via webhook and create the SFCC order record; Global-e owns the international checkout and payment layer | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-007 | Order Creation & Processing | The system will pass the selected delivery method to the OMS as a structured attribute; NewStore OMS maps this to the appropriate carrier and fulfilment route. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-008 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will display available delivery methods to the customer at checkout, sourced from configuration in SFCC Business Manager per storefront; available methods, display names, descriptions, and costs are configured per site. | Dependent SF Functionality | ALL | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-009 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will display an estimated delivery timeframe alongside each delivery method (sourced from Narvar CONVERT widget for domestic storefronts, or Global-e for international). | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-010 | Fulfilment & Delivery | ~~The system can apply free shipping thresholds per storefront as configured in Business Manager.~~ The system will support configurable free shipping thresholds in SFCC Business Manager, configurable independently per delivery method and per storefront. | Dependent SF Functionality | ALL | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-011 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will pass the customer's selected delivery method to the OMS via MuleSoft; NewStore OMS owns all downstream carrier selection, dispatch, and label generation. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-012 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will allow the customer to select a boutique and proceed to payment; full payment is required at placement for BOPIS orders. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| OM-013 | Fulfilment & Delivery | The system will pass the selected boutique ID and a 'collect from boutique' flag to NewStore OMS via MuleSoft; NewStore OMS owns all BOPIS fulfilment logic from this point. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custo