 confirmed rate card. | Accenture | EU Domestic | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| DLV-005 | Checkout Flow & Delivery | Delivery Method Configuration | The system will configure each delivery method in SFCC Business Manager with a unique ID, customer-facing name, description, tax class, and currency, independently per storefront. | Accenture | AU, UK (domestic), EU (domestic), US (domestic) | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| DLV-006 | Checkout Flow & Delivery | Delivery Method Configuration | The system will allow business users to enable or disable individual delivery methods per storefront via SFCC Business Manager without requiring a developer deployment. | Dependent SF Functionality | AU, UK (domestic), EU (domestic), US (domestic) | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| DLV-007 | Checkout Flow & Delivery | Delivery Method Configuration | The system will designate one default delivery method per storefront per currency in SFCC Business Manager; the default method will be pre-selected at the delivery step of checkout. | Accenture | AU, UK (domestic), EU (domestic), US (domestic) | Config | Confirmed | We should have the ablity to change to a new default option if we need to disable the default one temporarily - confirmed configurable |\n| DLV-008 | Checkout Flow & Delivery | Delivery Method Configuration | The system will configure Collect in Boutique as a shipping method with the Store Pickup Enabled flag activated in SFCC Business Manager, enabling the boutique selection flow at checkout. | Accenture | AU, UK (domestic), EU (domestic), US (domestic) | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| DLV-009 | Checkout Flow & Delivery | Estimated Delivery Date | The system will display a dynamic estimated delivery date (Narvar widget) window alongside each delivery method at the checkout delivery step (e.g. \"Estimated Delivery: Mon 12 May – Wed 14 May\"). | Accenture | AU, UK (domestic), EU (domestic), US (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| DLV-010 | Checkout Flow & Delivery | Estimated Delivery Date | The system will not support customer-selectable delivery date or time-slot selection at checkout at go-live; estimated delivery windows will be display-only and not customer-configurable. | Accenture | AU, UK (domestic), EU (domestic), US (domestic) | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| DLV-011 | Checkout Flow & Delivery | Delivery Cost Configuration | The system will support value-based tiered shipping costs per delivery method, configurable per storefront in SFCC Business Manager. | Dependent SF Functionality | AU, UK (domestic), EU (domestic), US (domestic) | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| DLV-012 | Checkout Flow & Delivery | Delivery Cost Configuration | The system will support a configurable free shipping threshold per delivery mode ~~storefront~~ in SFCC Business Manager; orders meeting or exceeding the threshold will qualify for free Express shipping. | Dependent SF Functionality | AU, UK (domestic), EU (domestic), US (domestic) | Config | Confirmed |  |\n| DLV-013 | Checkout Flow & Delivery | Carrier & Fulfilment Integration | The system will pass the customer-selected delivery method identifier to NewStore OMS via MuleSoft at order placement; carrier will be determined downstream by OMS/NewStore | Mule Integrator | AU, UK (domestic), EU (domestic), US (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| DLV-014 | Checkout Flow & Delivery | Carrier & Fulfilment Integration | The system will present a single delivery method selection to the customer at checkout; where an order is split into multiple shipments by NewStore OMS, this will be communicated post-purchase via Narvar and will not be presented as a split experience at the checkout delivery step. | Accenture | AU, UK (domestic), EU (domestic), US (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  |\n| DLV-015 | Checkout Flow & Delivery | Carrier & Fulfilment Integration | The system will not display carrier names (e.g. DHL, Australia Post, FedEx) to the customer at checkout; only the configured delivery method name and estimated delivery window will be shown. | Accenture | AU, UK (domestic), EU (domestic), US (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  |",
